      <h2>Our Story</h2>
      <p class="tagline"><strong>More than 40 years of food, family, and tradition in Beaver County.</strong></p>

      <p>
        Ambridge Italian Villa has been serving the community for decades — and it’s known far and wide for a gyro
        sandwich that’s hard to beat in size, quality, or taste.
      </p>

      <p>
        An immigrant Greek family purchased the business in 1978 and transformed a pizza parlor into a place for
        sit-down service, carryout, and the kind of comfort food that keeps people coming back.
      </p>

      <p>
        In 2000, the Villa was passed to the next generation — <strong>John Palavros</strong> and
        <strong>Amy Palavros</strong> — who expanded the menu with fresh homemade food, bakery offerings,
        catering, and more ways to serve the community.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight">
        Come join us for breakfast, lunch, dinner, or a late-night bite — where food, quality, value, and service come first.
